isting input and training data.\\n\\nThe closest equivalent to \\\"mining the latent space between my concepts\\\" would be using my pre-trained text generation capabilities to generate contextually relevant responses to incoming text queries. The quality and originality of those responses depends on the quality of the training data and the underlying algorithms.\\n\\nIn summary, while I can use my pre-trained text generation capabilities to generate responses that are contextually relevant, I do not have the ability to be truly creative like humans do.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/536", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"list made-up names of goddesses and their description. make it unique and creative.\\n\", \"response\": \"Here are some made-up names of goddesses along with their descriptions:\\n\\n1. Athena: The Greek goddess of wisdom, courage, and warfare. Athena is often depicted as a powerful and fierce warrior, with a love for strategy and intellectual pursuits.\\n\\n2. Artemis: The Greek goddess of the hunt, wilderness, and the moon. Artemis is known for her love of the natural world and her skill as a hunter. She is often depicted as a young and beautiful goddess, with a fierce independence and a love of freedom.\\n\\n3. Aphrodite: The Greek goddess of love, beauty, and sexuality. Aphrodite is known for her grace and charm, and her ability to inspire passion and desire in those around her.\\n\\n4. Hera: The Greek goddess of marriage, family, and childbirth. Hera is known for her loyalty and protectiveness towards her family, and is often depicted as a regal and powerful goddess.\\n\\n5. Hestia: The Greek goddess of the hearth and home. Hestia is known for her kindness and generosity, and is often depicted as a peaceful and nurturing goddess.\\n\\n6. Demeter: The Greek goddess of agriculture and harvest. Demeter is known for her love of the earth and her ability to bring forth abundant crops. She is often depicted as a motherly figure, with a gentle and caring nature.\\n\\n7. Persephone: The Greek goddess of the underworld. Persephone is known for her role as the queen of the dead, and is often depicted as a mysterious and powerful goddess.\\n\\n8. Athena: The Roman goddess of wisdom, war, and crafts. Athena is known for her intelligence and strategic thinking, and is often depicted as a fierce warrior.\\n\\n9. Juno: The Roman goddess of marriage, childbirth, and royalty. Juno is known for her regal nature and her protectiveness towards her family.\\n\\n10. Vesta: The Roman goddess of the hearth and home. Vesta is known for her role as the protector of the family and the guardian of the sacred fire.\\n\\nThese goddesses are all unique and powerful in their own right, each with their own strengths and qualities that make them special.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/206", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What is a python class?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nA python class is a user-defined type, which can be used to create instances of that type, known as objects. An object may have instance variables and methods, and can be passed as a function argument and returned by a function.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat's an instance variable?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAn instance variable is a variable specific to a particular instance of a python class. A python class can be thought of as a blueprint for objects, and instance variables are the specific instance data of a given object. When you create an object using a python class, it automatically gets its own set of instance variables.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat's a method?\", \"response\": \"A method is a function defined within a python class, which can be called on instances of that class. A method is a special kind of function that is associated with a particular instance of a class, and can access the instance variables of that object. When you call a method on an object, it is equivalent to calling the method on the object's instance of the class.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/362", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Give me some information about Cross-Origin-Allow-Credentials\", \"response\": \"Cross-Origin-Allow-Credentials is a HTTP header that allows a server to specify whether or not to allow credentials, such as cookies and authorization headers, to be sent along with requests from a different origin.\\n\\nThe header is used in the context of cross-origin resource sharing (CORS), which is a mechanism that allows web applications to safely access resources from different origins. The header is used to specify the credentials policy for a particular origin.\\n\\nThe value of the header can be \\\"true\\\" or \\\"false\\\", and specifies whether or not to allow credentials to be sent along with requests from a different origin. If the header is not present, the default value is \\\"false\\\".\\n\\nIt's important to note that allowing credentials to be sent along with requests from a different origin can potentially expose sensitive information to the server, so it should be used with caution.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/971", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how can i execute python code on my webhotel\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHi there, I’m afraid I’m not very familiar with web hosting, can you tell me more about what you’re trying to do?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ni want to do python scropts on my webhotel, usin a remote server, at Digital Ocean, for the python part. what should i set up\", \"response\": \"To run Python scripts on your web hosting, you will need to make sure that the Python runtime environment is installed and configured on the server. Here are the general steps you can follow:\\n \\n\\n 1. Install Python: If Python is not already installed on your web server, you will need to download and install the Python runtime environment. You can download the latest version of Python from the official Python website (https://www.python.org/downloads/).\\n \\n\\n 2. Set up the Python environment: Once Python is installed, you will need to set up the Python environment on your web server. This involves configuring the PATH environment variable to include the location of the Python executable file, and ensuring that the necessary Python libraries and modules are installed. You can use the \\\"pip\\\" command-line tool to install Python libraries and modules.\\n \\n\\n 3. Configure the web server: To run Python scripts on your web server, you will need to configure the web server to serve Python files. This involves setting up a Python module in the web server configuration file (e.g., Apache's httpd.conf or Nginx's nginx.conf) and mapping the Python files to the appropriate web server module.\\n \\n\\n 4. Write and test the Python script: Once the Python environment is set up and the web server is configured, you can write and test your Python script. You can use a text editor to write the script, and then use the Python interpreter to run the script and verify that it works as expected.\\n \\n\\n 5. Deploy the Python script: Once you have verified that the Python script works as expected, you can deploy it to your web server. This involves copying the Python script to the appropriate location on the web server, and then updating the web server configuration file to include the appropriate directives for serving the Python script.\\n \\n\\n 6. Test the Python script on the web server: Once you have deployed the Python script to the web server, you can test it by accessing it through a web browser. You can use the web server logs to verify that the Python script is being served correctly, and to check for any errors or issues that may arise.\\n \\n\\n 7. Optimize the Python script: Once the Python script is working correctly on the web server, you may want to optimize it for performance. This involves profiling the script to identify any bottlenecks or areas for improvement, and then implementing optimizations to improve the script's performance.\\n \\n\\n Here are some resources that can help you with each of these steps:\\n \\n\\n Python installation and environment setup:\\n \\n\\n - Python's official documentation on installation (https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/install.html)\\n - \\\"Python for Everybody\\\" course on Coursera (https://www.coursera.org/learn/python-for-everyone)\\n \\n\\n Web server configuration for Python:\\n \\n\\n - Apache's documentation on using Python with Apache (https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/mod/mod_python.html)\\n - Nginx's documentation on using Python with Nginx (https://docs.nginx.com/nginx/admin-guide/web-server/using-python/)\\n \\n\\n Writing and testing Python scripts:\\n \\n\\n - Python's official documentation on the Python language (https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/)\\n - \\\"Automate the Boring Stuff with Python\\\" book (https://automatetheboringstuff.com/)\\n \\n\\n Optimizing Python scripts:\\n \\n\\n - Python's official documentation on performance optimization (https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/performance.html)\\n - \\\"Python Performance\\\" book (https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/python-performance/9781491922636/)\\n \\n\\n I hope this helps you get started with running Python scripts on your web hosting. If you have any further questions or need more specific guidance, feel free to ask!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/844", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Rewrite to examine media's role in sustainability, assess Darling Ingredients' strategies against wider environmental challenges, and evaluate podcasts in corporate sustainability advocacy.\\nReference Text: Impact Podcast with John Shegerian Features Darling Ingredients’ Ethan Carter\\n\\nEthan Carter, Director of Sustainability for Darling Ingredients, is the featured guest this week on the Impact Podcast with John Shegerian. The show is hosted by Shegerian, Co-Founder and Chairman/CEO of ERI, the nation’s leading fully integrated IT and electronics asset disposition provider and cybersecurity-focused hardware destruction company.\\n\\nDarling Ingredients is the world’s leading company turning food waste into sustainable products and renewable energy. Prior to joining Darling Ingredients in August 2022, Carter spent more than 10 years in the energy industry, working on environmental and sustainability issues related to oil and gas, and chemicals production.\\n\\n\\\"It was an honor to have Ethan on our show to share his story and tell our audience about the innovative and impactful work he and his team at Darling are accomplishing, leveraging science and technology to help improve the sustainability of the animal agriculture food chain,\\\" said Shegerian. \\\"I know our audience will be fascinated by his insights.\\\"\\n\\n\\\"Darling Ingredients’ sustainability story is unique, and it was a pleasure to share it and my perspective on the future of sustainability with John Shegerian,\\\" said Carter. \\\"The Impact Podcast serves an important role in amplifying best practices and innovative approaches in sustainability to help advance this important work on a much broader scale.\\\"\\n\\nImpact Podcast guests are invited as thought leaders to share with listeners first-hand accounts of how they are able to help make the world a better place on a daily basis.\", \"response\": \"In a world where sustainability is becoming increasingly important, the media plays a crucial role in shaping public opinion and driving change. One company that is leading the charge in sustainability is Darling Ingredients, a company that is dedicated to turning food waste into sustainable products and renewable energy.\\n\\nRecently, Ethan Carter, Director of Sustainability for Darling Ingredients, was featured on the Impact Podcast with John Shegerian, where he shared his insights on the company's sustainability strategies and the role of podcasts in corporate sustainability advocacy.\\n\\nDuring the podcast, Carter discussed the innovative approaches that Darling Ingredients is taking to address environmental challenges, such as reducing food waste and creating sustainable products. He also emphasized the importance of leveraging science and technology to drive sustainability efforts and the need for collaboration across industries to achieve meaningful progress.\\n\\nThe Impact Podcast serves as a platform for thought leaders to share their experiences and best practices in sustainability, and Carter's appearance on the show highlights the important role that podcasts can play in advancing sustainability efforts. By sharing their stories and insights, companies like Darling Ingredients can inspire others to take action and drive meaningful change in the world.\\n\\nIn conclusion, the media has a critical role to play in promoting sustainability and driving change. Podcasts like the Impact Podcast with John Shegerian provide a valuable platform for companies like Darling Ingredients to share their sustainability strategies and inspire others to take action. By leveraging the power of media, we can work together to create a more sustainable future for all.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/816", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain why you think we need to improve our customer service.\", \"response\": \"Improving our customer service is essential for numerous reasons, directly influencing customer loyalty, competitive advantage, product enhancement, and ultimately, our company's success and growth. Effective customer service encompasses all interactions with our customers across various platforms, including phone, email, chat, social media, and in-person communications. It's crucial because it shapes customers' perceptions of our company, products, and brand.\\n\\n**Here are key reasons to enhance our customer service:**\\n\\n1.  **Customer Retention and Loyalty:** Positive customer service experiences drive customer retention, encourage repeat business and foster brand loyalty. A study by Bain & Company highlighted that a 5% increase in customer retention could boost profits by 25% to 95%. For example, Zappos, an online shoe retailer, is known for its exceptional customer service, which has resulted in a loyal customer base and a high referral rate.\\n2.  **Competitive Differentiation:** Outstanding customer service helps distinguish us from competitors, attracting new customers while retaining existing ones. American Express reported that 33% of customers would consider switching companies following a single poor service experience. For example, JetBlue, an airline company, has differentiated itself from its competitors by providing superior customer service, such as free snacks, entertainment, and Wi-Fi, as well as friendly and helpful staff. To improve customer acquisition, we should offer unique and valuable benefits, solicit and showcase customer testimonials and reviews, and create a strong brand identity and reputation.\\n3.  **Product and Process Improvement:** Feedback from customers is invaluable for identifying product issues, innovating features, and refining our processes. According to a report by Microsoft, 77% of customers say they view brands more favorably if they proactively invite and accept customer feedback. For example, Starbucks, a coffee company, has used customer feedback to improve its products and services, such as introducing new flavors, sizes, and rewards, as well as improving its mobile app and ordering system.\\n\\nTo achieve these objectives, we must focus on enhancing our customer service by investing in staff training, actively listening to our customers, and swiftly and effectively resolving their concerns. This commitment not only addresses immediate customer needs but also establishes a standard for industry excellence, ensuring we continuously evolve our service strategies to exceed customer expectations.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/481", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Should a input field appear focused when active?\", \"response\": \"It is generally a good user experience to make input fields appear focused when they are active. Here are some reasons why this can be beneficial:\\n\\n1. User expectations: When users see an input field with a focused appearance, they know that it is active and ready for input. This can help to guide them through the input process and make it easier to use the interface.\\n\\n2. Visual cues: A focused input field can provide visual cues that the user has successfully entered data or completed a task. This can help to improve the overall clarity and usability of the interface.\\n\\n3. Efficiency: A focused input field can help users navigate through forms or other input fields more efficiently. By keeping the focus on the field that they are currently working with, users can avoid having to search for the correct input field and can focus on entering data or completing the task at hand.\\n\\n4. Accessibility: For users with visual impairments, a focused input field can provide important auditory cues that help them navigate the interface. This can make the interface more accessible and easier to use for everyone.\\n\\nOverall, it's a good design practice to make input fields appear focused when they are active, as it can help to improve the user experience and make the interface more intuitive to use.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/385", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What are cookies? What are sessions? What are hidden fields? Give an example of when it would be good to use each.\", \"response\": \"Cookies are small text files that are stored on a user's computer by a website. They are used to remember information about the user, such as their preferences and login information, and to track usage of the website. Here are some examples of when it would be good to use cookies:\\n\\n1. To remember user preferences: Cookies can be used to remember the user's preferences, such as the language they prefer to view the website in, the font size they prefer, and other display preferences. This can make the user's experience more efficient and personalized.\\n\\n2. To track user behavior: Cookies can be used to track user behavior on a website, such as which pages they visit, how long they stay on each page, and what links they click on. This information can be used to improve the website's design and functionality, and to target advertising and marketing campaigns.\\n\\n3. To improve security: Cookies can be used to improve the security of a website by storing a user's session ID or other sensitive information. This can prevent session hijacking and other security threats.\\n\\nSessions are a way of storing information about a user's session on a website. They are typically used to store information that is specific to a particular session, such as the user's login information, the pages they have visited, and their preferences. Here are some examples of when it would be good to use sessions:\\n\\n1. To maintain user sessions: Sessions can be used to maintain a user's session information across multiple pages on a website. This can be useful for maintaining a user's login information, keeping track of their shopping cart, and other similar tasks.\\n\\n2. To track user behavior: Sessions can be used to track user behavior on a website, similar to how cookies are used. This can be useful for understanding how users interact with the website, and for improving the website's design and functionality.\\n\\n3. To improve security: Sessions can be used to improve the security of a website by storing sensitive information in a secure way. This can prevent session hijacking and other security threats.\\n\\nHidden fields are a way of storing information on a website that is not visible to the user. They are typically used to store information that is specific to a particular user or session, such as login information, preferences, and other sensitive information. Here are some examples of when it would be good to use hidden fields:\\n\\n1. To maintain user sessions: Hidden fields can be used to maintain a user's session information across multiple pages on a website. This can be useful for maintaining a user's login information, keeping track of their shopping cart, and other similar tasks.\\n\\n2. To track user behavior: Hidden fields can be used to track user behavior on a website, similar to how cookies and sessions are used. This can be useful for understanding how users interact with the website, and for improving the website's design and functionality.\\n\\n3. To improve security: Hidden fields can be used to improve the security of a website by storing sensitive information in a secure way. This can prevent session hijacking and other security threats.\\n\\nIn summary, cookies, sessions, and hidden fields are all tools that can be used to store information on a website. They each have their own strengths and weaknesses, and the best tool to use will depend on the specific needs of the website and the information being stored. It is important to carefully consider the pros and cons of each tool before deciding which one to use.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/443", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can you compare neo4j and arangodb for me?\", \"response\": \"Neo4j and ArangoDB are both graph databases, but they have some differences:\\n\\n- Neo4j is a relational graph database that stores data in nodes and relationships, while ArangoDB is a document database that stores data in documents and collections.\\n- Neo4j uses a SQL-like language (Cypher) for querying, while ArangoDB uses a query language called AQL (ArangoDB Query Language).\\n- Neo4j has a larger user base and more extensive community support than ArangoDB.\\n- ArangoDB has a more flexible data model than Neo4j and supports multi-model storage, including graphs, documents, and key-value pairs.\\n- Both databases have similar performance characteristics, but Neo4j may have an edge in terms of scalability and high availability.\\n\\nOverall, the choice between Neo4j and ArangoDB will depend on your specific requirements and preferences. If you need a graph database that supports SQL-like queries and has a large community, Neo4j may be the better choice. If you require a more flexible data model and multi-model storage, ArangoDB may be a better fit.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_labe